  "//": [
    "Never-tokenize list: ordinary Dutch and English words.",
    "",
    "Why this exists: a personal/org filter is built from vocabulary, and",
    "vocabulary collides with language. 'Kern', 'Boring', 'Post', 'Meet',",
    "'Bank', 'Water' are all real Dutch words AND plausible product or",
    "process names. Without this list, adding one to a pack silently",
    "tokenizes every ordinary use of it, which both mangles your text and",
    "tells Claude less than nothing.",
    "",
    "The allow-list wins over patterns AND explicit identifiers, because it",
    "is the thing you reach for when the filter is too eager. If you really",
    "do want a word tokenized, remove it here.",
    "",
    "Matching is case-insensitive and normalised, so one entry covers every",
    "casing. This is a starting point, not a dictionary - add what bites you."
  ],

